PART E  the dS / conformal-group route is blind to a0
  [OK] E1  substituting phi = sqrt(A0) psi turns  div(|grad phi| grad phi) = 4 pi A0 rho  into an A0-free equation: the deep-MOND symmetry group (dilatations, 10-parameter conformal group = SO(4,1)) is the same for every a0
      => the isomorphism 'conformal group of R^3 = isometry group of dS_4' relates two symmetry groups; it contains no relation between a0 and l_dS; xi in a0 = c^2/(xi l_dS) stays a matched O(1) number (Singh 2601.04290 sec 4).
  [OK] E2  CONTROL: the Newtonian operator (1/r^2) d/dr(r^2 phi') is NOT invariant under phi -> sqrt(A0) phi with A0 fixed by the source, so the A0-blindness is a property of the deep-MOND (cubic) sector, as Milgrom's scale-invariance argument says

